<article class="insight-card"><p class="eyebrow">WORKSPACE GUIDE</p><h2>A practical guide to EduPulse</h2><p>Start with the five KPI cards. Apply an academic year, semester, program, year level, or subject to inspect a smaller scope. Every report uses the same validated filters.</p><button class="btn-primary" type="button" data-tour-start>Start guided tour</button><h3>Understand the measures</h3><dl><dt>Course Pass Rate</dt><dd>100 × passed course units / attempted course units. Proposed target: at least 85%.</dd><dt>Students at Risk</dt><dd>100 × academic records with average grade above 3 OR attendance below 75% / selected academic records. Proposed maximum: 15%.</dd><dt>Teaching Effectiveness</dt><dd>Total SETE score / total criterion responses, weighted by responses. Proposed target: at least 4 / 5.</dd><dt>SETE Response Rate</dt><dd>100 × Clarity responses / Clarity invitations; one criterion avoids counting respondents repeatedly. Proposed target: at least 70%.</dd><dt>Grade Completion</dt><dd>100 × completed academic records / selected records. A period record is complete when all of its subject grades are complete. Proposed target: at least 95%.</dd></dl><h3>Read charts accurately</h3><p>Semester charts compare all periods using the selected program, year level, and subject. Current-period tables and cards use the selected year and semester. Subject passing and failing percentages include pending enrollments in the denominator.</p><h3>Use the right kind of evidence</h3><p>Public cohorts are synthetic and period-specific. Historical charts compare cohorts, not individual student trajectories. Subject-level risk flags and period-average risk flags answer different questions.</p><h3>SETE scope and model limits</h3><p>SETE is not attributable to individual subjects or year levels in this dataset. Those filters show unavailable teaching KPIs. The ML Risk Explorer uses a separate Portugal dataset and is not validated for CICS students.</p><h3>Data access</h3><p>Public views publish aggregated synthetic data only. Imports require server-side administration configuration. Institutional records remain excluded from the public dashboard and exports.</p></article>
